Diversity scripts rely on stack for analysis:
1. Install Haskell Stack. Download and install Stack for Windows from https://docs.haskellstack.org/en/stable/install_and_upgrade/
During install, allow Stack to install GHC and MSYS2 when prompted.
Once installed, open Command Prompt, PowerShell, or Git Bash, and run:
stack --version

2. Create a Workspace Directory
Organize your files so dependencies and source code are clear:
 
C:\Projects\
└── BCellDiversity\
    ├── diversity\          ← Clone the diversity repo here
    └── fasta\              ← Clone the fasta repo here
 
3. Clone Both Repositories
In PowerShell or Git Bash:
cd C:\Projects\BCellDiversity
git clone https://github.com/DrexelSystemsImmunologyLab/diversity.git
git clone https://github.com/GregorySchwartz/fasta.git

4. Pin fasta Dependency Locally
The diversity code depends on the fasta package, so you’ll need to point Stack to use your local version.
Modify diversity/stack.yaml to include the local path to fasta:

packages:
- .
- ../fasta

This tells Stack to treat the fasta directory as a local dependency.

5.1: Upgrade the Resolver (Recommended for Modern Stack)
You'll update the project to use a newer GHC version (e.g., lts-12.0), which will:
-Work with the current Stack version
-Require updating the fasta and diversity .cabal files to fix any package compatibility issues
This gives you a maintainable setup, even if it takes a bit of tweaking.
change:

yaml
resolver: lts-8.0
to:

yaml
resolver: lts-12.0

Step 5.2: Run Stack Setup
stack setup
This will install GHC 8.4.4 for lts-12.0.
 
6. Build the Project
After stack setup, try to  build everything: 
stack build
 
You will see an error: Your local fasta package depends on pipes-text >= 0.0, but no compatible version is included in the lts-12.0 resolver. 
Add pipes-text to extra-deps:
Open your stack.yaml in:
C:\Users\kconn\Bcelldiversity\diversity\stack.yaml
Add this block to the bottom, if extra-deps: doesn't exist already:
 
yaml
CopyEdit
extra-deps:
  - pipes-text-1.0.1@sha256:1cf1d24104a517a7c44d4c756b379757dede071319162201ac17ceb5c28a571c,3102
 
Then Try Building Again:
stack build
 
Building will take a while. The progress bar (Progress 0/63) showing up at the end is likely from Stack checking cached build tools or installing dependencies post-build — not an error.
7. Test the diversity Command
In PowerShell (still in the diversity folder):
stack exec -- diversity --help
 
This should work. 
